{
  "notable_events": [
    "The autumn harvest is the largest in a decade, filling the mill's granaries to bursting.",
    "A traveling merchant brings news that King Eldric has levied a new grain tax to fund his northern campaigns.",
    "The Stonehand miller, old Torvin, dies suddenly, leaving his son Garret to manage the mill.",
    "Duke Aldric's tax collectors arrive early, demanding a portion of the harvest before winter stores are set aside."
  ],
  "texture_line": "The air smells of cut grain and woodsmoke, but a tension hangs over the village as the duke's men tally the harvest."
}

